A||||8||fropuff||Gauge question||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||07-16-2001||01:33 AM||||Hey guys.  I've been thinking of getting some white-face gauges for my GT, but I've heard that Super X Motorsports went out of business??  Anyway, I was washing a newer Lincoln a while back, and I can't get over how sweet its gauges were.  When the ignition is in the "OFF" position, the gauges are all black and cannot be seen.  When the ignition is in the "ON" position, only the numbers and the needles can be seen, and are in white.  All else is black.  I want to do something like this, if it's possible.  Has anyone tried this?  Thanks!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||07-16-2001||11:31 AM||||I had an old girlfriend with a Mazda MX6 that was like that. During the day the gauges were white with black letters. At night they became black with white letters. Very cool but I have no idea how they did it..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||07-16-2001||11:37 PM||||That's exactly what I was thinking!  I wish someone knew how to do this.  Any help is appreciated.  Thanks a lot!<P>------------------<BR>If it ain't broke, might as well slap on some nitrous!||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||07-17-2001||11:45 AM||||I noticed that someone has a dutch auction on Ebay for the Stick on White Guage faces(Item # 593395165)... has anyone used these? I have an '87 GT and like the look of the white, but don't want to sacrifice too much visibility at night.<P>-Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||07-18-2001||01:08 AM||||Use Ausfiero's white face gause pattern, invert the white part. Cut the now white part off the top layer and cut out the colored part out of the second layer. Then you have to wire the gauge lights so they come on with the key and not the headlight switch. You would also have to find a clear needle for the gauges.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||07-18-2001||10:29 AM||||Is that for the white-faced, black letters, or the black-faced, white letters?  I'll have to go over to Aus's post and try to understand better.  Thanks for the help though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||07-18-2001||04:02 PM||||You take the white with black lettering and invert the colors so that the background is black and the numbers are white. Then cut out the numbers and the lines that are now white. For the second layer, the numbers should also be white or any color you want them really. and the background also black. Without the gauge backlighting on, everything should look black. With the lights on, everything that you cut out of the top layer and tht isn't black on the second layer should light up.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||07-20-2001||12:46 AM||||Okay, I think I understand!  Let's see though...I print out two of the same things; black-faced with white lettering.  On one of the two, I cut out the numbers and the other stuff that is white.  I leave the other one.  Then I stick the two together.  Then I run the gauge wiring to the ignition, so they're on when the ignition switch is?  I hope this will work.  I sat in a new 'Vette tonight, and the gauges are sweet!  They're kinda like what I want, but only with blue lettering and numbers.  I'm hoping I can do this.  I'll put up another post so I can ask about the wiring.  Thanks again for any help!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Have a good one! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||07-20-2001||01:08 AM||||Okay, I did a search for Aus's post, and I found a backlighting face w/ white lettering.  Okay, so I do a set of these three backwards, then flip them and print off another set normally?  Then I stick them together?  Thanks!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SpeedoBL.gif">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TachoBL.gif">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DashGaugesBL.gif"> ||||reg||1
